{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3295","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3295","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3295\",\"parent_revision\":\"542aff6d6e36422b108ee6afef367c4b98a710726785bcca7b024dc74d18da51\",\"root_revision\":\"542aff6d6e36422b108ee6afef367c4b98a710726785bcca7b024dc74d18da51\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-29\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nT6 (part of #3151's implementation) claimed to have \\\"demonstrated working end to end\\\" both the `PostToolUse` and `SubagentStop` hook dispatch paths through `skills/implementation-manager/scripts/task_status_hook.py`, citing 53 passing tests as evidence.\\n\\nThe orchestrator verified this claim and found it overstated: every one of those 53 tests calls the internal handler functions (`handle_subagent_stop`, `handle_activity_update`) directly, with the internal SAM-MCP subprocess call mocked. No test in the suite invokes `task_status_hook.py` itself as a real subprocess with hook-event JSON on stdin \u2014 the actual contract Claude Code uses to invoke it (per the script's own docstring: \\\"Receives JSON via stdin with hook context\\\").\\n\\nTraced `main()` (task_status_hook.py:961-988) and confirmed it's a thin dispatcher with no independent logic of its own \u2014 it parses stdin and calls exactly the two already-tested handler functions, and this entrypoint/`parse_hook_input()` were untouched by #3151's changes. So this is not a regression risk from that specific refactor, but it is a genuine, pre-existing test-coverage gap: nothing in the suite would catch a stdin-parsing or entrypoint-level regression in this hook script.\\n\\n**Hypothesis**: adding one integration test that shells out to the actual script (`uv run --script task_status_hook.py`) with a realistic hook-event JSON payload on stdin, for at least one non-local backend, would close this gap.\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Quality vigilance concern from #3151 \u2014 orchestrator observation while independently verifying T6's TN-verification claims during the SAM task-file-language refactor\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-29\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"6148a4cd32446447fd83142ca5ef97a0c8a1753cea0b8cb6a04927a47ac1aa2b\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABRZ5n9w\"}"}